{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6d461971413b29e13aa6de780592d6e79d453b1308a861ac4eacf1169117ac81","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"gabrielmaialva33/winx-code-agent@a48e7a9f7e86 snapshot 3dc3feafd9c47b9c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3a2409efce6f1abc32da7527c5d3b80e4839b18fb24d24e8b107b36271e3ff94","slc_44e4f1846afd41d712c5ab13577f775aa05e44461ca53b948bb4cdd029deb134"],"source_ids":["src_6ce5b3301cc853339f515f7626188d8c"],"text":"On Unix, the MCP adapter is separated from PTY-owning processes: winxd manages the control plane and one winx-guardian per session keeps shells alive across disconnects and adapter upgrades.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_be9e773f1613dfe0ba8f4a425042b68bc83be5f11c0ae3fcba71ea2e1d0128ab","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"gabrielmaialva33/winx-code-agent@a48e7a9f7e86 snapshot 3dc3feafd9c47b9c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5e0364828fc324fce09d337e41e2c494e3d5ca5ad13880d90411770855ec0de3"],"source_ids":["src_6ce5b3301cc853339f515f7626188d8c"],"text":"Winx advertises MCP 2026-07-28; every tool publishes an outputSchema and returns a structuredContent envelope whose authoritative status field enumerates states like completed, conflict, needs_read, and denied.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c76755fb1b3d5d067bce1993547f1583eb8a2554b909a991373d96dee48dbb01","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"gabrielmaialva33/winx-code-agent@a48e7a9f7e86 snapshot 3dc3feafd9c47b9c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_08fde4655742d1aee01952b5e7a56e4031f4aa946adf4bc51777a73693626c32","slc_eaf423b31b0d6ad0c36307a0cf499d20d8dccd4f517ca96dfca7bc1359ef8fbf","slc_fb659b1e4396f4c62b3c1207bc7c88436993d68786b425d3b430f92f41166f6b"],"source_ids":["src_6ce5b3301cc853339f515f7626188d8c"],"text":"The single mutation tool EditFiles supports replace, SEARCH/REPLACE, revision-bound line patches, atomic batches, verification, and undo, with legacy edit names kept as hidden compatibility aliases.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c8e4d665c37d330a8a24ba66bf52949e3d865968f2595414dd4a8a11446a144e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"gabrielmaialva33/winx-code-agent@a48e7a9f7e86 snapshot 3dc3feafd9c47b9c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cb3ef2abc9ad8145b3634a4ee4f1b1bd157376a786c84fbbe14aab98d48440ad"],"source_ids":["src_6ce5b3301cc853339f515f7626188d8c"],"text":"Workspaces have three modes: wcgw (full access), architect (read-only), and code_writer (command allowlist plus write globs), with the allowlist parsed via tree-sitter to check every command including pipelines and substitutions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ca797917cdac719391d5d6289ae7a93bf16460945d5ba98c6eb1925691caa934","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"gabrielmaialva33/winx-code-agent@a48e7a9f7e86 snapshot 3dc3feafd9c47b9c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_050757e7fd9b1a3104bd6edd87a1d4a3c903279ac623c8a2fad54f669936170f"],"source_ids":["src_6ce5b3301cc853339f515f7626188d8c"],"text":"MCP Tasks on BashCommand are capability-driven: adaptive promotes only after runtime state is running, until_complete creates a Task immediately, and return_early never does; cancellation is generation-bound with a fail-closed fallback.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899"}
